{% from 'ingressroute.yml.j2' import monitoring_route with context %}
---
{#
  ONE reader through this route: postflight.py's §9.3 API-key check, which asks for
  /api/v3/queue because it is the path this route admits. monitor-bridge's check_arr_queue
  (`monitor-bridge/files/checks/service.py`) reads RADARR_URL, a ClusterIP
  (`radarr.<ns>.svc.cluster.local:7878`), and never touches Traefik — the template comment said
  otherwise until 2026-09-10 (#1683), carried forward through two rewrites without being
  checked. Nothing else on the radarr API is reachable through this route.

  extra_client_cidrs admits the cluster nodes' own host processes, which is what postflight is,
  and `include_bridge_ip=false` drops the macro's default grant. That default is
  `k8s_bridge_client_ip` (10.0.0.161, daniel-server's LAN address), left over from when
  monitor-bridge was a Docker container ON daniel-server; it is dead on this route and was
  measured dead on 2026-09-10. A request from a daniel-server shell to
  `radarr.local.<domain>/api/v3/queue` arrived at Traefik as `ClientHost: 10.42.1.0` and got a 302,
  so the route did not match — 10.0.0.161 never reaches it.

  That measurement also bounds both grants. These are cluster-internal addresses, not the nodes'
  LAN addresses: host traffic to the ingress VIP SNATs to one of them, and which one depends on
  where the traefik POD sits. Traffic to a traefik pod on the SAME node stays on the local
  bridge and arrives as that node's cni0 gateway; traffic from the OTHER node crosses the VXLAN
  overlay and arrives as the SENDING node's flannel.1 address. Traefik is pinned to daniel-box
  (`kubernetes.io/hostname` nodeSelector), so daniel-box arrives as its cni0 gateway
  `10.42.0.1` — measured the same day, a 401 from radarr rather than a 302, which is the route
  matching and radarr rejecting the absent X-Api-Key — while daniel-server arrives as its
  flannel.1 address `10.42.1.0`, NOT as its cni0 gateway `10.42.1.1`.

  Both lists, therefore. The cni0 pair alone matches only while traefik sits on the node
  postflight runs on: moving the pod to daniel-server, or unpinning it, makes postflight's
  request arrive as `10.42.0.0`, which no clause grants, and §9.3 returns to the permanent SKIP
  that #1642 and #1675 were both filed to fix (#1697). Nothing ties the traefik nodeSelector to
  this route, so the route admits both address sets instead. Same variables and the same
  reasoning as loki-homelab's read route, whose `DECIDED 2026-08-24` marker verified the
  daniel-box half live first.

  The path prefix, the LAN-only rule and radarr's own X-Api-Key are unchanged.
#}
{{ monitoring_route(container_item.name, container_item.hostname, container_item.port, '/api/v3/queue',
                    extra_client_cidrs=k3s_cni0_gateways + k3s_flannel_node_ips,
                    include_bridge_ip=false) }}
